[gd_scene load_steps=9 format=3]

; A pal bed. A STAND-IN, and recorded as one.
;
; Same problem as the trainer's bed — the extracted kit has no furniture — and
; the same answer: honest primitive geometry at honest dimensions rather than a
; crate pretending. A straw mat in a low timber frame, 1.60 x 1.60m and 0.26m
; tall, inside one 2m build cell.
;
; Deliberately a DIFFERENT SILHOUETTE from `bed.tscn`: square instead of long,
; ankle-high instead of knee-high, no headboard. Two beds that read the same at
; a glance are two beds the player will build in the wrong place, and §20 lists
; "beds" and "pal beds" as separate categories.
;
; It is somewhere a pal sleeps. It is not a workstation and nothing about it
; should ever suggest a pal is working — see the hard-rule note in
; scripts/building/station.gd.

